# Review: BloggerPlugin

The data model, operations and sync are solid and well tested. `AddPublication` and `AddPost` run
through the operation invoker in `operations.test.ts`, and every reconciliation branch of `SyncPosts`
(push, update, revert, pull, `getDraft` fallback) is covered in `sync.test.ts` against a stub
publisher, matching scenarios T-1 to T-7. The weakest area is the navtree and toolbar wiring: the
Publications section, the "+ Publication" / "+ Post" actions, the comments companion and the Sync
enablement rule are implemented but no test drives them. The biggest divergence is `PostArticle`: it
renders only the body document; the name + outline form the spec places on top is not rendered there.
Both types use the `indigo` hue where the spec says `amber`.

Of 38 items: 23 done, 9 untested, 4 partial, 0 diverged, 2 missing (QA-1, QA-2).

## Extensions

| Term      | URI                        |
| --------- | -------------------------- |
| `verdict` | `org.dxos.mdl.verdict@1.0` |

